CHECKS.  SIBLING PARITY: the store arm is now rowed at len 1, 2, 3 (split head), 4, 8 and the read arm at 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
(split), 8 -- the table-1 asymmetry (reads only above len 2) is the finding this repair answers.  CLAIM -> ROW: the
contract's catch-list (rewritten) maps each item to a row named in the channel lines below; p_nozero, the dead `% len'
and the exit-after-fold are named EQUIVALENT in the header.  GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD: the edited `byte = data[ofs]'
is guarded by `writeflag == MEM_WRITE' as well as `len' (Opus Q3.5); p_wnarrow conjoins `len <= 2' onto it -- rowed.
CHANNEL (new rows): st4 lane3 (flat readback of an STL to SCR) -- p_wbit1, p_wnarrow, p_wdrop4, p_waddr4, g_len4w,
m_lane1; st8 lane3 -- the same + p_q8lane, m_nomask; st4 lane0 / ld4 lane0 -- p_lane0decl, p_wnarrow/p_wdrop4/p_waddr4
(store) and m_replicate/p_rep4 (full-register read); ld4 full -- p_rep4, m_replicate; ld8 lane3 -- follows st8 + read
decode; h3 ldq / h3 ldl -- HEAD (the fix-changed (3,3) read), m_andmask, m_decleq, m_writeonlyfold, m_lane1,
m_replicate, m_retzero; h5 ldq -- m_andmask, m_lane1, p_q8lane, m_replicate, m_retzero; split al -- m_nomask, m_lane1,
p_q8lane, m_replicate, m_retzero; h3 stq -- m_andmask, m_decleq, m_readonlyfold, m_lane1, p_wnarrow/p_wdrop4/p_waddr4.
OUT OF TABLE: p_port10 (an address-decode edit, not an edit of the fix; its split-tail outcome depends on what ISA port
0 answers, so no exact prediction can be written -- DISCLOSED in the header).

