NOTES ON THE HARDER PREDICTIONS.  p_waddr4 forwards an STL to MCR onto LSR (Opus: `lsr reads 0x62'): `ld4 full' is
predicted GREEN because its want is computed from the flat LSR read taken LATER in the same session.  m_lane1 at
SCR: (0x3ff & 1) % len = 1 for every width >= 2, so every SCR store at len >= 4 forwards position 1 (0x00) and every
SCR read packs at position 1 -- hence the whole split set.  m_nomask at SCR: 0x3ff % 3 = 0 and 0x3ff % 5 = 3 match
the fix, so only the len-8 SCR cells differ.  A red row outside its prediction is re-run ALONE before it is believed.
Load: two probe lanes; #529's closing-pass-4 panel may still be answering (reading seats only).
